## Wall-clock framing

Classical: measured seconds from the rows (T2b C port, single thread, 4 shards concurrently — times above ~45 s include contention). Range 0.8–126.9 s, median 24.4 s, total for the 56 rows 1635 s.
Quantum: Q Toffolis executed serially (the argmax route is inherently sequential: G Grover iterations, each a full reversible forward recursion) at 1 MHz and 1 GHz logical Toffoli rate. Median Q = 8.47e+12 → 8.47e+06 s at 1 MHz (0.268 years), 8.47e+03 s at 1 GHz. Fastest quantum row (largest p*): 2.27e+08 Toffolis = 227 s at 1 MHz. Slowest: 1.43e+23 Toffolis = 4.53e+09 years at 1 MHz, 4.53e+06 years at 1 GHz.
Rows where quantum wall-clock beats the measured classical seconds: 0/56 at 1 MHz, 15/56 at 1 GHz.

## Sensitivity

(a) Most quantum-favourable variant T3 listed (no certificate G = 9/√p*, no uncomputation — a lower bound, not a valid circuit): rows with Q_opt < C_new: 22/56; best speedup 5.35e+02 (T4/clean/P12); median 5.32e-02. Q_opt/Q = 2.14e-01 on every row (constant factor 9/42).
(b) Classical charged node-only (1 unit per generation, C_node = gen): rows with Q < C_node: 0/56; best speedup_node 4.46e-03; median 6.15e-07.
(c) Both at once (lower-bound circuit vs node-only classical): rows with Q_opt < gen: 0/56; best 2.08e-02.
(d) F11 tree-search route (reconstruction, see notes): rows with Q_tree < C_new: 0/56; best speedup 7.78e-02; Q_tree/Q_argmax median 1.47e+03.
